From cdf114803370b369bf2a37ba945d75b9d5597fc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hlib Hraif <hlib.hraif@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 19:07:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: engine - Fix use-after-free of backlog request

When the crypto engine queue is full and a new request arrives with
CRYPTO_TFM_REQ_MAY_BACKLOG, crypto_enqueue_request sets queue->backlog
to the new request and adds it to the queue. crypto_pump_requests then
retrieves the backlog via crypto_get_backlog() and removes the first
entry via crypto_dequeue_request(). However, if the backlog entry is not
the first entry, it remains in the queue's linked list while being
completed at the retry: label. The completion callback frees the
request, but the freed entry is still linked in the queue. When a
subsequent crypto_dequeue_request attempts list_del() on the freed
entry, it crashes with:

  list_del corruption, ->next is NULL
  kernel BUG at lib/list_debug.c:49!
  crypto_dequeue_request -> crypto_pump_work [crypto_engine]

Fix by removing the backlog from the queue before completing it, but
only if it was not already removed as the first entry.

Signed-off-by: Hlib Hraif <hlib.hraif@gmail.com>
---
 crypto/crypto_engine.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crypto/crypto_engine.c b/crypto/crypto_engine.c
index 34effd482..b9b8613bd 100644
--- a/crypto/crypto_engine.c
+++ b/crypto/crypto_engine.c
@@ -214,6 +214,18 @@ static void crypto_pump_requests(struct crypto_engine *engine,
 	crypto_request_complete(async_req, ret);
 
 retry:
+	/*
+	 * If the backlog entry was not the first entry removed by
+	 * crypto_dequeue_request() above, it is still linked in the queue.
+	 * Remove it before completing to prevent use-after-free when the
+	 * completion callback frees the request.
+	 */
+	if (backlog && backlog != async_req) {
+		spin_lock_irqsave(&engine->queue_lock, flags);
+		list_del(&backlog->list);
+		engine->queue.qlen--;
+		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&engine->queue_lock, flags);
+	}
 	if (backlog)
 		crypto_request_complete(backlog, -EINPROGRESS);
 
-- 
